 &lt;div class="main-content"&gt;
&lt;h2 id="minecraft-server-install-guide"&gt;Minecraft Server Install Guide:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="updating-the-system"&gt;Updating the system&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First step we want to do is make sure our Debian system is up to date.
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;apt update &amp;amp;&amp;amp; apt upgrade&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="setting-up-linux-user"&gt;Setting up linux user&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First thing we want to do is setup a non-root user that we can connect to via SSH and configure the linux server with:
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useradd -mU -s /bin/bash -G users,sudo &amp;lt;name&amp;gt; &amp;amp;&amp;amp; passwd &amp;lt;name&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open up another terminal or multiplexer and verify you are able to login via SSH.
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;ssh &amp;lt;user&amp;gt;@&amp;lt;ip-address&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ubuntumini</title><link>https://xorsirenz.github.io/blog/ubuntumini/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://xorsirenz.github.io/blog/ubuntumini/</guid><description>&lt;article class="main"&gt;
